WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
If your prep is SUPREP, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:03.760
.

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.520
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.400
Your bowel prep kit comes with two small bottles and a mixing container.

5
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.920
You'll use one bottle the evening before your procedure and the second bottle

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.880
the morning of.

7
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.080
You'll also need water.

8
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.520
For your first dose between 5 and 6 p.m. the evening before your colonoscopy,

9
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.700
pour the entire contents of the first bottle into the mixing container provided

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:25.920
.

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.810
Fill the container with water to the 16-ounce fill line and drink the entire

12
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:30.240
amount.

13
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:36.830
After you finish, continue to drink 16 to 32 ounces of clear liquids until you go

14
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.360
to bed.

15
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.360
Remember, do not drink red, orange, blue or purple liquids.

16
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.960
For your second dose, 7 hours before your procedure time,

17
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.720
pour the entire contents of the second bottle into the mixing container.

18
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.520
Fill with water to the 16-ounce fill line and drink the entire amount.

19
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.650
After finishing this second dose, drink an additional 32 ounces of water within 1

20
00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.200
hour.

21
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.640
Do not have any liquids at all within 4 hours of your procedure.

22
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.360
This part is really important.

23
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.760
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

24
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.040
passing clear liquid.

25
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.160
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

26
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:18.800
the clearest

27
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.540
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

28
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.880
need to reschedule,

29
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.440
and neither of us wants that. Staying hydrated throughout the process is key.

30
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.760
Make sure you're drinking plenty of clear liquids between your doses.

31
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.560
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

32
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.560
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

33
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.000
That's it, you've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

34
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.640
hydrated.

35
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.110
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

36
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:54.960
to help.
